WEBVTT

00:00:01.050 --> 00:00:03.410
Greetings, everyone.

00:00:03.780 --> 00:00:10.470
Today's ****** was ******* because 
of the ******* *************,

00:00:10.470 --> 00:00:13.520
so we have a ****** ******** 
special that's basically a *****!

00:01:55.040 --> 00:02:01.000
<b>Nothing Lasts Forever, Including Parents, Money, 
Youth, Your Room, Dress Shirts, Me, You, and the Gintama Anime</b>

00:02:01.550 --> 00:02:02.980
Uh, excuse me.

00:02:02.980 --> 00:02:04.250
I had no idea what you said

00:02:04.250 --> 00:02:05.760
at the beginning because of all the censoring.

00:02:05.970 --> 00:02:08.040
Read between the lines, Pachi-boy.

00:02:08.040 --> 00:02:10.050
Just look at what we're wearing.

00:02:10.050 --> 00:02:12.510
And a kotatsu in May?

00:02:12.890 --> 00:02:15.580
They're reusing old footage 
for this conversation.

00:02:15.580 --> 00:02:17.220
Eight episodes into the new show and

00:02:17.220 --> 00:02:18.350
we're already resorting to cheap tricks.

00:02:18.350 --> 00:02:20.130
And eight's supposed to be a lucky number?

00:02:20.140 --> 00:02:21.910
No wonder your name has 
Japanese word for eight in it.

00:02:21.910 --> 00:02:23.110
What's that supposed to mean?!

00:02:23.110 --> 00:02:26.000
The success of the movie led to the 
TV series returning after one year.

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:27.880
Everything was going too smoothly.

00:02:27.880 --> 00:02:29.740
This show is always on the 
verge of falling apart.

00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:32.530
The second series could end at any time.

00:02:32.530 --> 00:02:35.610
We might as well air the same episode 
eight times, starting next week.

00:02:35.610 --> 00:02:36.910
Since Shinpachi's name has 
the word for eight in it.

00:02:36.910 --> 00:02:38.790
We can't do that!

00:02:39.150 --> 00:02:41.040
And first, we have to figure out

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:42.570
what we're doing for the rest of this episode!

00:02:42.570 --> 00:02:45.570
If we keep reusing old footage 
while babbling about nothing,

00:02:45.570 --> 00:02:47.820
the producers who were 
so happy about the show

00:02:47.820 --> 00:02:50.260
coming back will have to go back to apologizing to everyone.

00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:52.920
Well, let's play a song for now?

00:02:52.920 --> 00:02:55.890
A song for the valiant efforts 
of Hasegawa-san, who's managed

00:02:55.890 --> 00:02:57.890
to survive despite his dark future, much like this show.

00:02:57.890 --> 00:02:58.520
Take it away.

00:03:02.600 --> 00:03:09.190
Cardboard...

00:03:02.600 --> 00:06:22.930
<b>"The God of Cardboard"
MADAO</b>

00:03:09.610 --> 00:03:17.290
Cardboard...

00:03:18.660 --> 00:03:21.750
They've taken everything away.

00:03:22.170 --> 00:03:25.560
My home, my job, my salary.

00:03:25.710 --> 00:03:29.300
I couldn't fight back

00:03:29.300 --> 00:03:32.260
as I lost everything.

00:03:32.550 --> 00:03:35.430
And then I...

00:03:35.930 --> 00:03:39.770
became a middle-aged dumb-ass oldie.

00:03:41.600 --> 00:03:44.560
They've taken everything away,

00:03:44.900 --> 00:03:48.190
but the God of Cardboard gives stuff to me.

00:03:48.530 --> 00:03:52.240
Cardboard can be transformed

00:03:52.240 --> 00:03:55.200
into a bed.

00:03:55.530 --> 00:03:59.040
At night,

00:03:59.040 --> 00:04:02.960
cardboard keeps away the cold.

00:04:04.250 --> 00:04:11.090
Cardboard...

00:04:11.420 --> 00:04:18.060
O, God of Cardboard.

00:04:18.510 --> 00:04:25.350
Cardboard...

00:04:25.810 --> 00:04:33.070
I softly closed my eyes and went to sleep.

00:04:50.460 --> 00:04:53.550
They've taken everything away.

00:04:54.050 --> 00:04:57.010
My pride, my savings, my assets.

00:04:57.590 --> 00:05:01.060
I couldn't fight back

00:05:01.060 --> 00:05:04.020
as I wore down.

00:05:04.270 --> 00:05:07.770
And then I...

00:05:07.770 --> 00:05:11.610
Was still a middle-aged dumb-ass oldie.

00:05:13.400 --> 00:05:16.410
They've taken everything away.

00:05:16.740 --> 00:05:20.370
But the God of Cardboard gives stuff to me.

00:05:20.370 --> 00:05:23.950
Cardboard can be transformed

00:05:23.950 --> 00:05:26.920
into a house.

00:05:27.330 --> 00:05:34.920
Cardboard keeps away prying eyes.

00:05:36.050 --> 00:05:42.810
Cardboard...

00:05:43.140 --> 00:05:49.860
O, God of Cardboard.

00:05:50.230 --> 00:05:57.240
Cardboard...

00:05:57.610 --> 00:06:04.750
I softly curled up into a ball.

00:06:06.210 --> 00:06:21.640
Cardboard...

00:06:27.160 --> 00:06:29.620
Who exactly benefited from this?

00:06:31.440 --> 00:06:34.980
<b>Special Announcement</b>

00:06:35.900 --> 00:06:39.450
<b>The Gintama Movie Production Committee</b>

00:07:21.110 --> 00:07:22.520
Is this the end?

00:07:23.210 --> 00:07:25.400
Instead of falling into enemy hands,

00:07:26.100 --> 00:07:27.950
we should finish this like warriors

00:07:29.360 --> 00:07:31.860
and cut open our bellies.

00:07:33.200 --> 00:07:35.100
Don't be a fool.

00:07:37.430 --> 00:07:38.460
Stand.

00:07:43.030 --> 00:07:46.260
If you have time to plan out a pretty death,

00:07:46.990 --> 00:07:50.680
why not live a pretty life to the very end?

00:07:56.410 --> 00:07:58.050
Let's do this, Zura.

00:07:58.050 --> 00:07:59.320
It's not Zura.

00:08:01.060 --> 00:08:02.200
It's Katsura.

00:08:02.970 --> 00:08:07.720
The man's silver hair was lined with blood.

00:08:13.520 --> 00:08:17.500
He tore across the battlefield...

00:08:20.210 --> 00:08:21.300
...like a Yaksha.

00:08:21.300 --> 00:08:23.970
<b>Gintama the Movie II</b>

00:08:23.970 --> 00:08:29.220
<b>Birth of the White Yaksha</b>

00:08:26.680 --> 00:08:29.220
<b>Preview</b>

00:08:36.280 --> 00:08:39.130
This blessed land

00:08:39.130 --> 00:08:42.550
should not be wasted on those barbaric apes!

00:08:43.490 --> 00:08:44.780
Charge!

00:08:46.200 --> 00:08:48.700
Kiheitai! Follow my lead!

00:08:55.880 --> 00:08:57.980
You just charged in by yourself.

00:08:57.980 --> 00:08:59.590
You crazy in the head?

00:08:59.590 --> 00:09:01.510
You shouldn't be talking.

00:09:02.500 --> 00:09:03.670
Got that right.

00:09:04.300 --> 00:09:05.200
Here.

00:09:06.920 --> 00:09:09.430
Need a hand, Gintoki?

00:09:09.670 --> 00:09:10.860
Shut up!

00:09:10.860 --> 00:09:13.180
I don't need your help!

00:09:21.430 --> 00:09:22.470
I've made up my mind.

00:09:23.150 --> 00:09:25.040
I'm going into space.

00:09:25.860 --> 00:09:30.540
This war is killing off my friends.

00:09:31.700 --> 00:09:32.960
I'm sick of...

00:09:33.410 --> 00:09:36.290
...watching friends die.

00:09:48.980 --> 00:09:50.230
I see...

00:09:50.740 --> 00:09:53.820
You were the one who...

00:10:00.310 --> 00:10:01.080
Gintoki!

00:10:01.080 --> 00:10:03.980
This guy is mine!

00:10:04.180 --> 00:10:05.170
Tsk!

00:10:05.170 --> 00:10:06.950
Back off!

00:10:06.950 --> 00:10:08.060
Shut up!

00:10:31.780 --> 00:10:33.080
Ma...

00:10:34.790 --> 00:10:39.290
Master Shoyo!

00:10:37.940 --> 00:10:42.400
<b>This is when it all began.</b>

00:10:43.770 --> 00:10:47.190
<b>Coming next spring.</b>

00:10:47.190 --> 00:10:52.160
<b>Also screening:
Shinsengumi
- Arrival in Kyoto -</b>

00:10:52.160 --> 00:11:00.420
<b>Preorder Bonus
Everyone who preorders their tickets will receive Elizabeth 3D glasses!</b>

00:11:01.620 --> 00:11:04.680
Man, I didn't expect the second movie

00:11:04.680 --> 00:11:06.780
to cover this storyline.

00:11:06.780 --> 00:11:07.880
You bet.

00:11:07.880 --> 00:11:09.120
They're following up the success of

00:11:09.120 --> 00:11:12.840
Gintama the Movie: Benizakura Arc the New Translation.

00:11:12.840 --> 00:11:15.810
And this isn't a rehash of one 
of the arcs from the TV series.

00:11:15.810 --> 00:11:18.620
This is a completely original story.

00:11:18.620 --> 00:11:21.600
No one thought that the fake movie scam

00:11:21.600 --> 00:11:24.570
from Jump Anime Tour 2008 would become real.

00:11:24.850 --> 00:11:26.610
Grown-ups are scum.

00:11:26.610 --> 00:11:29.610
They're quick as lightning to ride on

00:11:29.610 --> 00:11:31.690
the coattails of success.

00:11:31.810 --> 00:11:33.320
Fastest in the world, or so they claim.

00:11:33.320 --> 00:11:36.130
At this rate, we can do a movie every year.

00:11:36.130 --> 00:11:37.310
If this one is an original story,

00:11:37.310 --> 00:11:39.730
the next one can be another remake of a TV arc.

00:11:39.730 --> 00:11:41.510
After "Birth of the White Yaksha,"

00:11:41.510 --> 00:11:43.510
we can do "Kagura and the Steel Troops."

00:11:43.510 --> 00:11:45.140
That arc doesn't exist!

00:11:45.140 --> 00:11:46.960
And you clearly copied that 
title from someone else!

00:11:47.290 --> 00:11:51.560
Oh, I'm pretty sure that the 
audience has noticed by now.

00:11:51.560 --> 00:11:53.060
Huh? Noticed what?

00:11:53.060 --> 00:11:56.540
Well, we're sitting here talking 
about a second movie...

00:11:58.140 --> 00:11:59.890
...but it ain't gonna happen.

00:12:00.930 --> 00:12:04.650
Life ain't easy for this series.

00:12:06.000 --> 00:12:08.150
I knew it.

00:12:10.800 --> 00:12:12.120
Wait!

00:12:12.120 --> 00:12:14.810
Stop lying through your teeth!

00:12:14.810 --> 00:12:18.150
We had a successful movie run 
and the series is back on TV,

00:12:18.150 --> 00:12:19.910
and you're still trying to pull that crap?!

00:12:20.080 --> 00:12:23.700
The successful movie only made 
1/4 of what One Piece did.

00:12:24.870 --> 00:12:26.090
You know...

00:12:26.090 --> 00:12:29.320
The success of Gintama the Movie: 
Benizakura Arc the New Translation

00:12:29.320 --> 00:12:30.990
was somewhat because we spent

00:12:30.990 --> 00:12:34.290
four years lying about making a movie on the TV show.

00:12:34.290 --> 00:12:36.090
We aren't big daddies here.

00:12:36.090 --> 00:12:37.500
Can't plant our seed on an annual basis.

00:12:37.500 --> 00:12:39.400
What kind of metaphor is that?!

00:12:39.400 --> 00:12:42.810
So we'll need to spend time 
setting up the next movie.

00:12:44.530 --> 00:12:47.610
In three years, when the next World Cup is.

00:12:48.280 --> 00:12:49.680
Though this show might not make

00:12:49.680 --> 00:12:52.190
it past the preliminaries for movie consideration.

00:12:53.390 --> 00:12:56.530
You guys aren't even trying, are you?

00:12:57.480 --> 00:12:58.980
Chief.

00:12:58.980 --> 00:13:02.580
Either way, the second movie 
won't use this storyline.

00:13:02.840 --> 00:13:03.700
Okita-san.

00:13:03.700 --> 00:13:05.820
Birth of the White Yaksha?

00:13:05.820 --> 00:13:11.340
The Shinsengumi will look even worse.

00:13:11.770 --> 00:13:13.120
Exactly.

00:13:13.120 --> 00:13:14.890
So if there's a second movie,

00:13:14.890 --> 00:13:17.950
it should be "Gintama the Movie: Okita Becomes a Sadist,

00:13:17.950 --> 00:13:19.810
Hijikata Dies in the Wasteland."

00:13:19.810 --> 00:13:21.290
What kind of subtitle is that?!

00:13:21.290 --> 00:13:23.010
Why are you kind of copying 
the title from someone else?!

00:13:23.010 --> 00:13:24.480
Why are you killing me off?!

00:13:24.780 --> 00:13:26.160
Calm down, Toshi.

00:13:26.160 --> 00:13:29.080
It doesn't matter if three years 
pass until the next movie.

00:13:29.080 --> 00:13:30.830
It doesn't matter if we 
don't play a major part.

00:13:30.830 --> 00:13:32.740
We will stay the course and

00:13:32.740 --> 00:13:34.960
stand upright like true samurai!

00:13:34.960 --> 00:13:37.070
You need to change your course!

00:13:37.200 --> 00:13:38.090
Wait!

00:13:38.090 --> 00:13:40.690
Why are you naked again?!

00:13:40.690 --> 00:13:44.230
Well, in a movie, an actress is

00:13:44.230 --> 00:13:47.040
supposed to provide a nipslip or, I mean,

00:13:47.040 --> 00:13:48.610
a little sexual tension!

00:13:48.610 --> 00:13:49.170
Kondo-san!

00:13:49.350 --> 00:13:50.710
S-Sis!

00:13:50.710 --> 00:13:52.580
Please, Shin-chan.

00:13:52.580 --> 00:13:54.350
We don't need any more movies

00:13:54.350 --> 00:13:55.740
after the Benizakura Arc movie

00:13:55.740 --> 00:13:58.580
where I was somewhat the main heroine.

00:13:58.580 --> 00:14:00.220
How selfish can you be?

00:14:00.710 --> 00:14:03.030
I strum a melody for Otae-chan.

00:14:03.030 --> 00:14:04.280
There is no other way.

00:14:04.280 --> 00:14:06.060
What are you talking about, Kyubei-san?!

00:14:06.290 --> 00:14:07.430
Boss lady!

00:14:07.430 --> 00:14:08.800
Let me be the heroine next--

00:14:14.110 --> 00:14:15.840
In the TV series, I may play a fool,

00:14:15.840 --> 00:14:18.740
but in the movies, I cut a dashing figure!

00:14:19.120 --> 00:14:22.910
All according to the law of movie-Gian!

00:14:22.910 --> 00:14:24.620
Takeshi!

00:14:25.460 --> 00:14:27.710
Wait up, Takeshi!

00:14:28.200 --> 00:14:30.260
Oh, sorry about that.

00:14:30.260 --> 00:14:33.920
The title of the next movie is 
"MADAO and the Steel Troops."

00:14:36.440 --> 00:14:37.840
It was a lie?

00:14:38.130 --> 00:14:40.140
I want to have a go at being the heroine.

00:14:40.140 --> 00:14:42.620
Then the three of us can be the 
main characters of the next movie,

00:14:42.620 --> 00:14:43.870
"Three for the Kill."

00:14:43.870 --> 00:14:45.430
I'll play Sengoku...

00:14:45.580 --> 00:14:47.370
You can't satisfy me by making me an extra!

00:14:47.370 --> 00:14:48.940
Stop it, stupid!

00:14:48.940 --> 00:14:50.400
I am Gian!

00:14:50.400 --> 00:14:51.810
You stupid bully!

00:14:51.810 --> 00:14:52.840
Hey!

00:14:52.840 --> 00:14:53.750
What the hell's going on?!

00:14:53.750 --> 00:14:55.090
How are we supposed to stop this circus?!

00:14:55.090 --> 00:14:56.270
How would I know, fool?!

00:14:56.620 --> 00:14:59.820
Man, look at you all whining.

00:14:59.820 --> 00:15:06.700
<b>Quit Smoking</b>

00:15:00.840 --> 00:15:03.590
That's why you're One Piece Quarter.

00:15:03.590 --> 00:15:06.700
Actually, it took four years 
to make 1/4 the amount.

00:15:07.910 --> 00:15:10.110
So if you want to be number one,

00:15:10.780 --> 00:15:12.840
you'll have to spend sixteen years preparing.

00:15:12.840 --> 00:15:13.710
Huh?

00:15:14.190 --> 00:15:15.960
What kind of logic is that?

00:15:16.260 --> 00:15:18.470
Hey, Luffy Quarter.

00:15:18.470 --> 00:15:19.220
Huh?

00:15:19.220 --> 00:15:20.270
Finish this.

00:15:20.270 --> 00:15:20.870
Hey!

00:15:20.870 --> 00:15:21.610
That's impossib--

00:15:21.610 --> 00:15:22.430
Bye.

00:15:22.430 --> 00:15:23.470
Don't run away, dammit!

00:15:24.000 --> 00:15:26.720
Wh-What do we do, Gin-san?

00:15:29.790 --> 00:15:30.980
Can't help it.

00:15:31.230 --> 00:15:32.600
Everyone gather round!

00:15:32.600 --> 00:15:35.150
We'll have to go with that!

00:15:37.000 --> 00:15:38.760
Here we go!

00:15:39.180 --> 00:15:40.520
Three!

00:15:40.520 --> 00:15:41.700
Two!

00:15:41.940 --> 00:15:44.660
One Peace!

00:16:02.800 --> 00:16:05.160
Ask Mr. Ginpachi!

00:16:05.160 --> 00:16:08.100
Is back!

00:16:08.100 --> 00:16:10.070
Okay, it's been a while.

00:16:10.070 --> 00:16:13.300
Let's go straight to the first question.

00:16:13.300 --> 00:16:16.220
From someone with the pen name YNG:

00:16:16.700 --> 00:16:19.900
In episode 197, "Not Losing to the Storm",

00:16:19.990 --> 00:16:23.490
there was a scene where 
Gin-san was hit in the balls.

00:16:23.720 --> 00:16:27.870
I'm a girl, so I don't 
know how much that hurts,

00:16:27.870 --> 00:16:29.190
but a certain person said that

00:16:29.190 --> 00:16:32.380
"it hurts as much as a direct ignore-defense attack

00:16:32.380 --> 00:16:33.830
on the abdominal area after a body blow

00:16:33.830 --> 00:16:37.840
removed all of the abs and other protection down there."

00:16:38.100 --> 00:16:39.940
I don't understand what that means.

00:16:39.940 --> 00:16:43.330
Could you give me a simple 
explanation of how much it hurts?

00:16:43.330 --> 00:16:45.940
This question has been 
keeping me up at night.

00:16:47.550 --> 00:16:49.950
Okay, here's your answer.

00:16:50.310 --> 00:16:52.920
Abdominal area without 
any abs makes no sense.

00:16:53.220 --> 00:16:54.820
Since you have abs,

00:16:54.820 --> 00:16:56.320
but no balls,

00:16:56.320 --> 00:16:57.770
it's hard to understand.

00:16:58.210 --> 00:17:01.240
I'll use a metaphor that's more romantic

00:17:01.240 --> 00:17:03.700
so the girls will understand.

00:17:03.850 --> 00:17:04.910
Now, let us pretend

00:17:05.320 --> 00:17:10.480
that you are drinking tea 
in a field of flowers.

00:17:10.790 --> 00:17:14.870
And then your pet bunny escapes.

00:17:14.870 --> 00:17:18.280
You run after it,

00:17:18.280 --> 00:17:20.880
but a prince on a white 
horse happens to pass by.

00:17:20.880 --> 00:17:24.310
However, he doesn't have 
enough time to react,

00:17:24.310 --> 00:17:26.980
and the white horse stomps on you.

00:17:26.980 --> 00:17:30.880
However, you were wearing 
a helmet, so you're fine.

00:17:30.880 --> 00:17:35.240
But then the prince loses his 
balance and is thrown off the horse

00:17:35.240 --> 00:17:38.160
and is about to hit the ground,

00:17:38.160 --> 00:17:40.150
when your butler catches him in mid-air

00:17:40.150 --> 00:17:41.880
since your butler used to be a gymnast.

00:17:41.880 --> 00:17:45.760
But since your butler strained 
himself, his back gives,

00:17:45.760 --> 00:17:49.690
leaving him in excruciating pain.

00:17:49.690 --> 00:17:51.390
Your butler screams in pain.

00:17:51.390 --> 00:17:53.510
But then he wakes up.

00:17:53.510 --> 00:17:57.220
Yes, it was all his dream

00:17:57.220 --> 00:18:01.440
in a crappy book that left you in pain

00:18:01.440 --> 00:18:03.340
and your mother in more 
pain as she watches you,

00:18:03.340 --> 00:18:06.380
and your father in even more pain 
after he accidentally hit his balls.

00:18:06.380 --> 00:18:07.280
That kind of pain.

00:18:10.890 --> 00:18:15.470
After a long suspension, he's finally back.

00:18:15.940 --> 00:18:21.770
Yes, bringing chaos and 
destruction back to class 3-Z...

00:18:23.180 --> 00:18:25.440
I simply destroy.

00:18:26.420 --> 00:18:27.920
Heartless and hardcore.

00:18:27.920 --> 00:18:30.600
Takasugi-kun!

00:18:31.080 --> 00:18:34.330
<b>Final Episode</b>

00:18:31.730 --> 00:18:32.530
Hey.

00:18:32.970 --> 00:18:34.330
Close your textbooks.

00:18:34.550 --> 00:18:37.110
Now, Mr. Kakashi from class N

00:18:37.110 --> 00:18:39.830
had his Sharingan stolen after school yesterday.

00:18:40.330 --> 00:18:43.090
There are quite a few suspects,

00:18:43.090 --> 00:18:46.870
but it's too much effort so I'm going 
to pick someone from this classroom.

00:18:47.200 --> 00:18:49.970
Does anyone know anything?

00:18:49.970 --> 00:18:52.720
Teach! Takasugi-kun looks suspicious!

00:18:53.200 --> 00:18:56.180
He must be hiding the Sharingan 
under that eye patch!

00:18:56.300 --> 00:18:59.610
He wants to copy my Ninja Centerfold!

00:18:59.910 --> 00:19:01.360
Is that true, Takasugi?

00:19:01.650 --> 00:19:04.260
Kondo's centerfold is just above his hairy ass.

00:19:04.260 --> 00:19:06.540
You'll only be copying a bunch of ass hair.

00:19:07.310 --> 00:19:09.740
Heh, who would want that?

00:19:10.220 --> 00:19:11.680
There you have it.

00:19:11.680 --> 00:19:15.360
Well, I understand why the delinquent 
Takasugi would be a suspect,

00:19:15.360 --> 00:19:19.000
but he doesn't need the Sharingan 
to improve his image.

00:19:19.240 --> 00:19:22.990
After all, Takasugi already has 
plenty of emo kiddie tendencies,

00:19:22.990 --> 00:19:26.740
such as being a delinquent, 
wearing an eye patch,

00:19:26.740 --> 00:19:28.360
and having a desire to destroy everything.

00:19:28.360 --> 00:19:30.760
You want me to destroy you?

00:19:31.320 --> 00:19:34.810
Well, I recommend that you refrain 
from picking up new personality traits

00:19:34.810 --> 00:19:38.190
to boost your popularity 
in the character rankings.

00:19:38.190 --> 00:19:42.020
You'll only confuse the audience 
by adding to your character.

00:19:42.670 --> 00:19:45.550
New additions frequently fail hard.

00:19:45.550 --> 00:19:47.650
It happens all the time in anime sequels.

00:19:47.870 --> 00:19:48.910
That's right.

00:19:48.910 --> 00:19:50.800
Those characters tend to be written off

00:19:50.800 --> 00:19:52.550
at the end of the second season.

00:19:53.320 --> 00:19:55.800
Teach, I feel sick.

00:19:55.800 --> 00:19:57.560
Can I go to the nurse's office?

00:19:57.900 --> 00:19:58.910
Shimura.

00:19:59.160 --> 00:20:01.450
You're going straight to the faculty office.

00:20:01.420 --> 00:20:03.420
<b>The End</b>

00:20:08.790 --> 00:20:11.320
And so, did you enjoy the 
Celebrating the 8th Episode

00:20:11.320 --> 00:20:13.950
of the New Series with Another Boring Recap Special?

00:20:13.950 --> 00:20:14.960
Next week's episode will be

00:20:14.960 --> 00:20:17.270
Celebrating the 9th Episode of the New Series with Another Recap.

00:20:17.290 --> 00:20:18.390
The hell it will!

00:20:18.620 --> 00:20:19.450
And yeah...

00:20:19.450 --> 00:20:20.860
If you're curious about next week,

00:20:20.860 --> 00:20:22.820
stick around after the ending credits.

00:20:22.820 --> 00:20:24.300
Are you talking about Piramekino?

00:20:24.300 --> 00:20:25.110
No!

00:20:25.110 --> 00:20:27.360
If we aired a recap this week 
and Piramekino next week,

00:20:27.360 --> 00:20:28.860
it wouldn't be a joke anymore!

00:20:28.860 --> 00:20:31.590
The show would be on the verge of fading out!

00:20:31.590 --> 00:20:32.780
Now, now.

00:20:32.780 --> 00:20:35.810
In any case, as long as nothing happens,

00:20:35.810 --> 00:20:37.010
same time next week.

00:20:37.010 --> 00:20:38.490
Be there!

00:22:05.460 --> 00:22:08.460
<b>Preview</b>

00:22:06.000 --> 00:22:07.070
What?

00:22:07.070 --> 00:22:09.880
You want to know who the strongest 
person in the Kabuki District is?

00:22:10.470 --> 00:22:13.710
There are four monsters 
on a level of their own.

00:22:14.210 --> 00:22:16.810
The Fierce and Divine Mademoiselle Saigo.

00:22:17.090 --> 00:22:19.550
Jirocho Doromizu the Gallant.

00:22:19.860 --> 00:22:21.480
Peacock Princess Kada.

00:22:21.800 --> 00:22:23.680
Empress Otose.

00:22:24.050 --> 00:22:28.040
The Kabuki District Four Devas

00:22:26.730 --> 00:22:30.940
<b>The Kabuki District Four Devas Arc</b>

00:22:28.040 --> 00:22:30.630
are in control of the Kabuki District.

00:22:31.450 --> 00:22:34.560
I have come to join Odd Jobs.

00:22:34.560 --> 00:22:35.820
My name is Pirako Chin.

00:22:35.820 --> 00:22:37.410
Huh?! A killer?!

00:22:36.070 --> 00:22:40.740
<b>The arrival of one girl...</b>

00:22:37.410 --> 00:22:38.630
This little twit?!

00:22:38.630 --> 00:22:41.290
This little girl works for the underworld?!

00:22:41.030 --> 00:22:45.160
<b>Signals trouble for the Kabuki District -</b>

00:22:41.340 --> 00:22:44.950
I only know how to decorate with flowers.

00:22:44.950 --> 00:22:47.000
I'm here to turn the town where Jirocho is...

00:22:47.290 --> 00:22:51.040
To turn the Kabuki District 
into a garden of bright red!

00:22:51.150 --> 00:22:54.360
There is no reason for us to fight.

00:22:51.250 --> 00:22:57.550
<b>Four factions -</b>

00:22:54.360 --> 00:22:58.050
After all, isn't our enemy Jirocho?

00:22:58.260 --> 00:23:02.600
<b>In an all-out war.</b>

00:22:58.800 --> 00:23:02.850
You bastards ready to have 
your balls ripped out?!

00:23:02.850 --> 00:23:04.720
<b>Jirocho Doromizu the Gallant</b>

00:23:05.220 --> 00:23:10.190
<b>drops in unexpectedly.</b>

00:23:06.130 --> 00:23:11.360
You think you can take 
my balls by teaming up?

00:23:11.690 --> 00:23:15.190
I don't have any members in my faction.

00:23:13.480 --> 00:23:18.610
<b>Emotions intertwine...</b>

00:23:16.040 --> 00:23:19.850
They serve no use at all.

00:23:16.860 --> 00:23:18.860
<b>I'm sick of waiting for you to pay the rent. Take your fools and scram. Never come back to this town.
-Otose</b>

00:23:19.850 --> 00:23:21.490
They just happen to be...

00:23:21.490 --> 00:23:23.240
...my family.

00:23:23.370 --> 00:23:26.100
Gran!

00:23:26.100 --> 00:23:27.650
So you're the White Yaksha?

00:23:26.120 --> 00:23:30.920
<b>Two warriors who refuse to back down...</b>

00:23:28.210 --> 00:23:30.920
There are plenty more like you out there.

00:23:34.630 --> 00:23:36.910
Crush us if you can.

00:23:36.910 --> 00:23:38.600
The Otose Family will

00:23:39.050 --> 00:23:41.770
be paying our respects.

00:23:41.140 --> 00:23:44.970
<b>A Lawless Town Tends to Attract 
a Bunch of Whoohooey Folk</b>
